{"kelime":"بندق","maddeler":[{"w":"بندق","u":"بندق","p":"noun","t":"From Middle Persian pndk' (pondik, “hazelnut”), from Ancient Greek Ποντικὸν κάρυον (Pontikòn káruon, “Pontic nut”). From hazelnuts, the sense spread to similarly shaped pebbles used in slings and similar projectile weapons and then to early muskets. In some dialects, the word then came to be used for the slingshots and muskets themselves.","s":[["etymon","[Appendix:Glossary#loanword|Borrowed]] from\", \"terms\" : [ { \"transliteration\" : \"pondik\", \"children\" : [ { \"keyword_abbrev\" : \"bor.\", \"keyword_label\" : \"Borrowed from\", \"terms\" : [ { \"children\" : [ { "],["bor","Middle Persian pndk' (pondik, “hazelnut”)"],["der","Ancient Greek Ποντικὸν κάρυον (Pontikòn káruon, “Pontic nut”)"],["etymon",""]],"g":["hazelnut","bullet","gun, rifle"],"tag":["Yemen","archaic","collective","dialectal","historical"],"r":["bunduq"],"ipa":["/bun.duq/"],"ds":[["xaa","بندق","bunduq"],["acw","بندق","bundug"],["am","ቡንዱቅ","bunduḳ"],["hy","պնդուկ","pnduk"],["fr","bonduc",""],["gez","መንዱቅ","mänduḳ"],["fa-cls","بَنْدُق","bunduq"],["fa-cls","فندق","funduq, fanduq"],["fa-cls","بَنْدُوق","bundūq"],["gdq","məndáwḳ",""],["shv","məndíḳ",""],["sw","bunduki",""],["tig","መንዱቅ","mänduḳ"]],"dr":["بُنْدُقِيَّة","كَسَّارَة بُنْدُق"],"el":[["Black Sea","Black Sea"],["Pontus","Pontus"],["-ic","-ic"],["pndk'","pndk'#Middle_Persian"],["hazelnut","hazelnut"],["Ποντικὸν κάρυον","Ποντικὸν κάρυον#Ancient_Greek"],["Pontic","Pontic"],["nut","nut"]],"yol":""}]}